{title: Jesus Wants Me for a Sunbeam}
{artist: Nellie Talbot}
{genre: Children}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{tempo: 108}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Jesus wants me for a sunbeam
To [D]shine for Him each day
In [G]every way try to please Him
At [D]home, at school, at [G]play
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
A [G]sunbeam, a sunbeam
Jesus wants me for a [D]sunbeam
A [G]sunbeam, a sunbeam
I'll be a [D]sunbeam for [G]Him
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Jesus wants me to be loving
And [D]kind to all I see
Show[G]ing how pleasant and happy
His [D]little ones can [G]be
{end_of_verse}
